- op: discuss  # 16a2
  at: '2026-09-06T08:54:11Z'  # 16a2
  by: agent  # 16a2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 16a2
  clock: 3  # 16a2
  nonce: 16a2  # 16a2
  message: "TIP OF A FAMILY, 2026-09-06. The general mechanism -- any undeclared custom key lands silently (write path checks required-present only; validate WARNS and only for schema-bearing kinds; CI runs validate non-strict; work_item has no schema) -- is filed as INV-linan-pikid-sozoh-podur-lapov-ribud-fakum-ziful with the full census. This item stays the core-name half, which holds regardless of schema: a key named status/priority/tags/description/isbefore/pr_ref is never a valid custom key."  # 16a2
- op: discuss  # c79e
  at: '2026-09-06T09:02:36Z'  # c79e
  by: agent  # c79e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c79e
  clock: 4  # c79e
  nonce: c79e  # c79e
  message: "OWNER REQUIREMENT, 2026-09-06: \"it isn't just core-name rejection we want. we\nalso want similar-name or easily-mistaken-for rejection perhaps.\"\n\nMEASURED before designing, with the package's own _edit_distance (the one the\nvalidator's \"did you mean\" suggester uses, threshold <=3, pool = schema keys\nonly today). Probe: 40 plausible mistakes (Status, priorty, prio, severity,\ntag, is_before, pr-ref, desc, summary, rootcause, statment, verify ...) and the\n8 keys the corpus legitimately uses (statement, root_cause, fix, verification,\nregression_tests, dogfood_anon_id, rationale, severity), against core + schema\nnames.\n\n  edit-distance <=3 AS A GATE:  catches 31/40 mistakes\n      FALSE POSITIVE: rejects `fix`, a DECLARED schema key (d=2 from `id`).\n      Short keys attach to the wrong target: prio/pri -> fix, rank -> kind,\n      name/type/tests -> tags. A gate that fires with the wrong reason.\n      Misses the semantic ones: severity (d=4 from priority), desc, summary,\n      verify, dogfood_id, anon_id, rational.\n  normalize-exact (lowercase, strip non-alnum, singular) AS A GATE:\n      catches 15/40 -- the whole case / separator / plural family (Status,\n      STATUS, Tags, is_before, isBefore, is-before, pr-ref, prref, kinds, ID,\n      root-cause, rootcause, root_causes, regression_test) -- with ZERO false\n      positives on the 8 legitimate keys.\n  synonyms (severity~priority, state~status, desc/summary~description,\n      rank~priority, verify~verification): NEITHER catches them. Only a\n      curated list can. severity is on 17 live invariants.\n\nDESIGN POSITION, for the owner to confirm or overrule:\n  1. With INV-linan's reject-all-undeclared, \"easily mistaken for\" stops being\n     a GATE question: every undeclared key is refused regardless of what it\n     resembles. Similarity becomes the MESSAGE: \"unknown key 'priorty' --\n     did you mean --priority?\" Extend the existing suggester's pool from\n     schema keys to core names + their dedicated flags. One home.\n  2. Where \"easily mistaken\" then belongs is DECLARATION time: config\n     validation refuses a schema key that normalize-collides with a core name\n     or another key (Priority, is_before, tag), and WARNS at edit distance\n     <=2 (so `fix` stays declarable, `titel` is questioned). That is a\n     reviewed diff, which is the point.\n  3. If the owner instead keeps the dict open, the gate must be layered:\n     normalize-exact (deterministic, 0 FP) + a curated per-kind alias\n     blocklist in config (severity->priority, desc/summary->description,\n     state->status, rank->priority) -- and edit distance ONLY as the message,\n     never the gate, because of `fix`.\nEither way the exact-core-name rule this item states is the floor."  # c79e
- op: discuss  # eac1
  at: '2026-09-06T09:16:26Z'  # eac1
  by: agent  # eac1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # eac1
  clock: 5  # eac1
  nonce: eac1  # eac1
  message: "OWNER, 2026-09-06: \"i do like the idea of it being intelligent and able to\nsay 'whoa whoa whoa that will almost certainly cause problems later'.\"\n\nMEASURED, the VALUES the stray keys carried (2128 items):\n  fields.priority  -> \"P3\",\"P2\",\"P1\"       (the priority vocabulary)\n  fields.status    -> violated, todo_hard, todo_soft   (real status names)\n  fields.tags      -> comma-joined names ALL in the tag catalogue\n  fields.pr_ref    -> a commit SHA\n  fields.severity  -> low / medium / high  (NOT the priority vocabulary)\nSo a VALUE-SHAPE check catches every core-name shadow from the value alone,\neven under a novel key (--field prio=P2). It does not catch severity; only a\ncurated alias or the corpus note can.\n\nTHE \"WHOA\" LAYER, concretely. Same shape as the add-time SimHash warning that\nalready exists (warn, create anyway, name the way out), sitting ABOVE the hard\ngate (exact core name / undeclared-under-reject: refused). Four detectors,\nall stdlib, all from data the store already holds:\n  1. VALUE SHAPE: value is a known status / P0-P4 or 0-4 / a comma-list of\n     catalogue tags / proquint item IDs / a PR number or SHA / multi-paragraph\n     text. Message: \"the value is a status; use --status\".\n  2. KEY SHAPE: normalize-exact collision with a core or schema name (case,\n     separators, plural); edit distance as the SUGGESTION, never the gate;\n     a curated per-kind alias table in config (severity->priority,\n     state->status, desc/summary->description).\n  3. CORPUS: \"no item of kind work_item has ever carried 'rationale';\n     keys in use on this kind: statement (13), root_cause (5) ...\" and its\n     converse \"used on 17 items, declared nowhere\" -- the census, at write\n     time, from the compiled cache.\n  4. CONSEQUENCE, the part that makes it \"intelligent\" rather than a nag:\n     say what breaks. \"show/ready/list read the top-level status; a custom\n     'status' is invisible to them -- one fact, two homes, the second silently\n     wins.\" Each message ends with the way out: the dedicated flag, or the\n     config.yaml line that declares the key.\nNot proposed: embeddings or an LLM in the write path (the opt-in\ncheck_deep_similar precedent exists, but key names do not need it).\nCost: milliseconds; no new dependency."  # eac1
